@startuml
title UML State Transition Diagram for Digital Watch

state "Normal Time Display" as NormalDisplay
state "Adjustment Mode" as AdjustmentMode
state "Alarm Off" as AlarmOff
state "Alarm On" as AlarmOn
state "Light Off" as LightOff
state "Light On" as LightOn
state "Alarm Ringing" as AlarmRinging

NormalDisplay : entry/Initial state
NormalDisplay : do/Display current time
NormalDisplay : exit button pressed to adjust settings

AdjustmentMode : entry/User presses adjust button
AdjustmentMode : do/Cycle through settings (Hour, Minute, Alarm Hour, Alarm Minute)
AdjustmentMode : exit button pressed to confirm or exit

AlarmOff : entry/Default state
AlarmOff : do/No alarm active
AlarmOff : exit/Turn on alarm by user action

AlarmOn : entry/User turns on alarm
AlarmOn : do/Alarm time set and active
AlarmOn : exit/Alarm time reached or turned off

LightOff : entry/Default state
LightOff : do/Light feature disabled
LightOff : exit button pressed to turn light on

LightOn : entry/User presses light button
LightOn : do/Light feature enabled
LightOn : exit button released to turn light off

NormalDisplay --> AdjustmentMode : Adjust button pressed
AdjustmentMode --> NormalDisplay : Exit adjustment mode
AdjustmentMode --> AlarmOff : Set alarm off
AdjustmentMode --> AlarmOn : Set alarm on
AdjustmentMode --> LightOn : Turn light on during adjustment
AdjustmentMode --> LightOff : Turn light off during adjustment

AlarmOff --> AlarmOn : Enable alarm
AlarmOn --> AlarmRinging : Alarm time reached
AlarmRinging --> NormalDisplay : Stop button pressed
AlarmRinging --> AlarmOff : Disable alarm while ringing

LightOff --> LightOn : Press light button
LightOn --> LightOff : Release light button

[*] --> NormalDisplay : Initial state

@enduml
